# Cypress tests (Fernly)

## 1. Queries

Prefer `findByRole`, then `findByLabelText`, then `findByText`. Never CSS modules or raw tag names.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — QuantityStepper exposes aria-labels on its buttons
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).click();
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — QuantityStepper.module.css `.button` is not a contract
cy.get('.button').last().click();
cy.get('button').contains('+').click();
```

## 2. States

Assert disabled, checked, or value on the element you already found. Chaining `.should('be.disabled')` on `findByRole` can fail with "Unable to find", which looks like a broken locator when the state is wrong.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).then(($btn) => {
  expect($btn, 'Increase quantity at stock limit').to.be.disabled;
});
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — same locator, misleading failure when + stays enabled (see FINDINGS stock-limit suspicion)
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).should('be.disabled');
```

## 3. Waiting

Never fixed delays. Wait on an intercepted `/api/*` alias or on what the user sees.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — Browse loads via GET /api/plants
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants*', { fixture: 'plants/catalog-positive.json' }).as('plants');
cy.visit('/');
cy.wait('@plants');
cy.findByText('Monstera Deliciosa');
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
cy.visit('/');
cy.wait(500);
```

## 4. Data

Component tests pass props at mount time. UI tests load API bodies from `web/cypress/fixtures/` — one file per scenario (positive, negative, edge).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — component: props only
cy.mount(<QuantityStepper value={3} max={3} onChange={cy.spy()} />);
```

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — UI: fixture per scenario
cy.fixture('plants/catalog-empty.json').then((body) => {
  cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants*', body).as('plants');
});
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — huge inline JSON in the spec
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants*', { plants: [/* … */] });
```

## 5. Mocks

`cy.intercept` only `/api/*` traffic, always with an alias. Never stub the page bundle or `cy.visit` HTML.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants/pl-monstera', { fixture: 'plants/pl-monstera.json' }).as('plant');
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
cy.intercept('GET', '/', '<html>fake shop</html>');
cy.intercept('GET', '**/BrowsePage*', { fixture: 'fake-page.json' });
```

## 6. Tags

Exactly one level tag per test: `{ tags: '@component' }` or `{ tags: '@ui' }`. A confirmed product bug may add `@known-bug` (excluded from CI via `grepTags=-@known-bug` in `package.json`).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
it('disables − at the minimum', { tags: '@component' }, () => { /* … */ });
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
it('browse loads', { tags: ['@ui', '@component'] }, () => { /* … */ });
describe('Browse', { tags: '@ui' }, () => { /* … */ });
```

## 7. App code

Do not change `web/src` to green a test. If behavior matches `docs/PRODUCT.md` and the app differs, record it in `FINDINGS.md` (see README: report defects, don't fix the shop).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — failing test + FINDINGS entry pointing at PRODUCT.md
// Evidence: web/cypress/component/QuantityStepper.cy.tsx — disables + at the stock limit
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — patching QuantityStepper.tsx so value > max becomes value >= max
```

## 8. Evidence

FINDINGS must say how you know: **executed** (test name), **inspected** (steps/requests), or **not yet tested** (suspicion).

```markdown
// ✅ GOOD — FINDINGS.md format
- **Evidence:** web/cypress/ui/browse.cy.ts — shows empty catalog message (executed)
```

```markdown
// ❌ BAD
- **Evidence:** Browse probably broken
```
